{"name":"Savannah Red","hex":"#a36159","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"savannah","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of savanna."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/savannah"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Savanna","blocks":[{"text":"A savanna or savannah is a mixed woodland-grassland biome and ecosystem characterised by the trees being sufficiently widely spaced so that the canopy does not close. The open canopy allows sufficient light to reach the ground to support an unbroken herbaceous layer consisting primarily of grasses. Four savanna forms exist; savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy; tree savanna, with scattered trees and shrubs; shrub savanna, with distributed shrubs; and grass savanna, where trees and shrubs are mostly nonexistent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Tarangire-Natpark800600.jpg/330px-Tarangire-Natpark800600.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savanna","wikidata":"Q42320"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg/500px-Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg/1280px-Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg/500px-Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A grass savanna at Kruger National Park in South Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASavanna_Grasslands_(199168845).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Australian_savanna.jpg/330px-Australian_savanna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Australian_savanna.jpg/330px-Australian_savanna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A savanna woodland in Northern Australia demonstrating the regular tree spacing characteristic of some savannas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAustralian_savanna.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Bushfire_Australia.jpg/500px-Bushfire_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig